<title>UK: Nigerian Qua Iboe, Oso oil output normal - Mobil.</title>
<headline>Nigerian Qua Iboe, Oso oil output normal - Mobil.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Production of Qua Iboe crude oil and Oso condensate in Nigeria are normal despite unrest that has forced output cuts elsewhere in the country, said a spokesman for equity producer Mobil Corp in Lagos.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not had any problems. Production is normal,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Last year the combined output of the two fields averaged 523,000 barrels per day. Current production is about 600,000 bpd, about 500,000 bpd of Qua Iboa and 100,000 bpd of Oso condensates, he said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom, 542 4984</p>
</text>
